      "title": "THEORY",
      "kind": "proposed",
      "page": 1,
      "text_preview": "Using natural sampling to produce PWM outputs is a wellknown technique [1], [2]. Comparing an input signal to a triangle wave will generate PWM data at the output of the comparator. If all elements of the natural sampling system in Fig. 3 (inside box) are ideal, the resulting PWM data will Fig. 3. Natural sampling with error correction feedback system. only have energy corresponding to the input s ..."
