    {
      "number": "V",
      "title": "CIRCUITS",
      "kind": "design",
      "page": 3,
      "text_preview": "In order to simplify the design as much as possible, the majority of the design uses an internal LDO regulator derived power supply of 1.4 V that must deliver an average current of 1.7 mA. Since this design is targeted for SOC applications, regulated and low-voltage supplies are readily available. This guarantees that there are no reliability problems for these circuits. Shown in Fig. 7 is the sim ..."
