      "kind": "results",
      "page": 5,
      "text_preview": "M5 and M6 form a positive feedback loop that increases the over all speed of the ﬁrst stage. M7–M9 create the output stage which must drive the power PMOS gate without voltage overstress. In order to limit the voltage swing, the transistor M8 is inserted. M8 will turn off when the output node swings such that of M8 falls below a . Therefore, must the be chosen prudently in order to protect the pow ..."
