      "title": "TESTING CHALLENGES",
      "kind": "other",
      "page": 6,
      "text_preview": "When testing inherently nonlinear systems such as class D, great care must be taken so that the collected data which characterize the performance of the design is not limited by the test setup. The highly nonlinear PWM output waveforms of the class D create problematic out-of-band energies. These energies can interfere with sampled data collection methods and easily produce confusing results in th ..."
    },
    {
      "number": "VIII",
      "title": "CONCLUSION",
      "kind": "conclusion",
      "page": 7,
      "text_preview": "A 700-mW Class D power ampliﬁer with direct battery connection has been presented. It achieves , 70-dB PSRR at 217 Hz, 55-dB CMRR up to 20 kHz, and 102-dBv SNR. The idle power consumption is 1.7 mA from the LDO supply and 3 mA from the battery. The performance achieved is with a default 90-nm digital CMOS process. The processing includes no mask or costly additional processing steps. The area of t ..."
